<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-6896] .NET: support Multidimensional Arrays in binary serializer</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-6896</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;It is found that legacy 2D, 3D, etc. are not working in BinarySerializer.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Sample reproducer:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
        [Test]
        &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;public&lt;/span&gt; void TestXX()
        {
            &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; array2D = &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;float&lt;/span&gt;[32, 32];
            &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; res = TestUtils.SerializeDeserialize(array2D);
            Assert.AreEqual(array2D, res);
        }
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;BTW, please note that 2D array in Java (a&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;2&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;2&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;) is just a jugged array:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;obj = {byte[2][]@1928}
 0 = {byte[2]@1974}
 1 = {byte[2]@1975}
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
